      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if the jitteriness feels minor, combining thyroid issues and stimulants like Adderall can put extra strain on your cardiovascular system. While it might not be an immediate emergency, continuously taking the same dose could increase the risk of more significant heart issues over time. Please call your doctor's office and explain your urgency, asking if a nurse or physician's assistant can provide interim advice over the phone. They can advise you on whether an immediate dosage adjustment or change in schedule is necessary.",
      "source": "target",
